Subject: [PATCH] [upstream] input: avoid hiding keyboard on window focus loss

Original change's description:
> input: avoid hiding keyboard on window focus loss
>
> Before:
> https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eoPck8UzHkU78VfczJR9drtnYX71spMi/view?usp=sharing
>
> After:
> https://drive.google.com/file/d/15tpX7oiLRlo5ZgQGt2fe2loCoDuyKNdW/view?usp=sharing
>
> Previously, CL 8363405 added if (!gainFocus) resetAndHideKeyboard(); in
> ImeAdapterImpl.onWindowFocusChanged() to fix b/558115274. However,
> calling resetAndHideKeyboard() on window focus loss causes the IME to
> immediately dismiss when focusable system dialogs or overlays open above
> Chrome while the activity remains top-resumed (e.g. IME picker dialog,
> notification shade, power menu) (b/560321831).
>
> To fix b/560321831 while preserving the fix for b/558115274: 1. Remove
> `if (!gainFocus) resetAndHideKeyboard();` on window focus loss so the
> keyboard remains visible when opening system dialogs/overlays, and
> replace with `reset()` (so that the keyboard does not disappear).
>
> 2. In updateState(), ensuring restartInput() is invoked to reconnect the
> system IME even if the focused editable DOM node ID did not change.
>
> Bug: b:560321831, b:558115274, b:570312518
